.TH CWE-269 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-269 \- Improper Privilege Management
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not properly assign, modify, track, or check privileges for an actor, creating an unintended sphere of control for that actor.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB19\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2014\-3153
Linux Kernel, added 2022\-05\-25.
.PP
Linux Kernel Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
The futex_requeue function in kernel/futex.c in Linux kernel does not ensure that calls have two different futex addresses, which allows local users to gain privileges.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-06\-15.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2014\-3153
